**/*
!package.json
!src/**
!lib/**
!icon.png
!README.md
!node_modules/highlight.js/package.json
!node_modules/highlight.js/lib/**
!node_modules/highlight.js/styles/*.css
.vscode/**

# What ships and why:
#
# The extension runs unbundled: src/ is the entry (main points at
# src/extension.js) and lib/ carries the generated CJS grammar that
# sync.rip byte-gates against packages/highlight.
#
# highlight.js ships as a real directory. printer.js requires
# 'highlight.js' at runtime, locates its themes with
# `require.resolve('highlight.js/package.json')` — so that file is the
# resolution anchor — and then READS `styles/<theme>.css` by computed
# path, which no bundler can inline.
#
# The styles are NOT narrowed to printer.js's themeList. An allowlist
# here would have to be kept in step with that array by hand, and
# loadThemes() skips a missing stylesheet silently — so drift would cost
# a theme with no error anywhere.
